# System account for the eForm render browser.
#
# Declared by THIS package rather than carlos-emr, together with the directory it
# owns (carlos-emr-eform-renderer.tmpfiles). Splitting them across packages does
# not work: dh runs sysusers before tmpfiles WITHIN a package, but carlos-emr is
# configured first on a clean install, so its tmpfiles would try to create a
# carlos-render-owned directory before this package's sysusers had created the
# account — "Failed to resolve user 'carlos-render': Unknown user".
#
# In NO group, deliberately, including not `carlos`. chromedriver has no
# authentication and any local uid can reach a loopback port, so an exposed one is
# an arbitrary-code-execution service running as whatever account started it. As
# `carlos` that would be the uid owning the patient document store and the database
# credentials; as carlos-render it owns nothing but a scratch home.
u carlos-render - "CARLOS EMR eForm render browser" /var/lib/carlos-emr/render /usr/sbin/nologin
